SUMMARY:Well Rooted: Genealogy Drop In
DESCRIPTION:Are you hitting a "brick wall" in your family tree research? Wh
 ether you are a seasoned researcher or just starting to wonder about your 
 heritage\, the library is here to help! Join us on the 3rd Thursday of eve
 ry month at 3:00 PM for our Genealogy Drop-In Program. Our volunteers will
  be on hand to help you navigate databases\, interpret census records\, an
 d organize your findings. If you have a specific research goal or a partic
 ularly tricky question\, we encourage you to reach out to us ahead of time
 . Providing details in advance allows us to prepare resources specifically
  for your search. Send us an email at info@mtpl.info When: 3rd Thursdays a
 t 3:00 PM Where: Morgan Center B Cost: Free and open to the public\n\nPric
 e: Free\n\nSchedule listed: Thu\, Nov 19\, 2026 03:00 PM EST – Thu\, Nov
  19\, 2026 04:30 PM EST\n\nSchedule supplied by Lancaster Libraries\n\nTim
 es converted from America/New_York to UTC for calendar compatibility.\n\n\
 n\nRegistration: https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/well-rooted
